{"study_accession":"PRJNA1418759","secondary_study_accession":"SRP674583","title":"Transcriptomes of clonally explanded human effector Gamma9Delta2 T cells","description":"In this study dedicated to the transcriptional, phenotypic and functional diversity of the human Gamma9Delta2 T cells we probed an array of in vitro-generated clones maintained using rapid expansion protocol (REP) which involves repetitive exposure to feeder cells, IL-2 and IL-15. Based on functional readouts in co-cultures with tumor cells we identified gradients of type 1 and, unexpectedly, type 2-like functionalities among the clones maintained in these type 1-polarizing conditions. Functional readouts were supported by in-depth transcriptional profiling. A gradient of activation, supposedly partially driven by VGamma9VDelta2TCR signaling, appears to shape this transcriptional and functional heterogeneity. Stronger activation drives a type 1-oriented state, marked by a signature IFNgamma response, enhanced proliferation, and polyfunctionality - traits that are particularly valuable for immunotherapy applications.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":11,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN55061686","study_accession":"PRJNA1418759","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"D145","description":"D145","sex":"not applicable","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-02-23","attributes":[["isolate","Sample-2"],["age","not applicable"],["biomaterial_provider","Kuball lab, CTI"],["collection_date","2016-01-27"],["geo_loc_name","Netherlands: Utrecht"],["sex","not applicable"],["tissue","Peripheral blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR37107562","experiment_accession":"SRX32053716","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"PCR","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":26306049,"base_count":1985597748,"first_public":"2026-02-23","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: D145"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_acc